            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "That figure is usually floor area, and you coat walls. A basement with 1,000 square feet of floor is roughly 25 by 40 feet, giving a 130-foot perimeter and about 1,040 square feet of wall at 8 feet. On standard block at two coats that is roughly 24 gallons, or five pails. On smooth poured concrete it is closer to 19."
